    "intro_html":  "Smothered chicken is Southern cooking at its most practical. You dredge the chicken in seasoned flour, brown it, build a roux gravy in the same pan with the drippings, then put the chicken back and let it finish in the gravy. Nothing gets wasted and nothing gets dry. It is also one of the best reheating dishes there is, because the gravy protects the meat all week. Each bowl carries 670 calories and \u003cstrong\u003e53 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e$1.42 a serving\u003c/strong\u003e.",
